1. e4 e6 2. d3 d5 3. Nd2 c5 4. Ngf3 Nf6 5. g3 Be7 6. Bg2 O-O 7. O-O Nc6 8. Re1 b5 9. Qe2 {(Keene, in "Flank Openings," gives this move a "?", saying that it should be reserved for replying to ?c7 - JS)} Bb7 $2 (9... Qb6 $145 10. c3 b4 11. e5 Nd7 12. c4 Qd8 13. Nb3 a5 14. cxd5 exd5 15. e6 Nf6 $2 (15... Nb6 $13) 16. exf7+ Kh8 (16... Rxf7 17. Ng5 Rf8 18. Ne6 $18) 17. Be3 a4 18. Nxc5 d4 19. Nxd4 Nxd4 {1-0 Dgebuadze,A-Hrubant,I/Mlada Boleslav op 1993}) (9... b4 $145 10. e5 Nd7 11. Nf1 a5 12. h4 Ba6 13. Bf4 a4 14. c4 $6 bxc3 15. bxc3 Rb8 16. Rac1 $2 a3 17. h5 Rb2 18. Rc2 Qc7 19. h6 $15 {Gierse,H-Uhlmann,W/Dresden op 1995/0-1 (31)}) (9... Rb8 10. e5 Nd7 11. Nf1 a5 12. h4 b4 13. Bf4 Ba6 14. Ne3 Qb6 (14... Nb6 {? ?a4 is worth some thought - Keene}) 15. Bh3 Rfd8 16. h5 $2 c4 $1 17. h6 (17. Qd2 c3 $1) 17... cxd3 18. cxd3 g6 19. Ng4 Nd4 $1 20. Nxd4 Qxd4 $17 {Samadov-Steinberg/USSR Jun Tch 1966/0-1(35)}) 10. Nf1 a5 11. e5 Nd7 12. h4 b4 13. N1h2 a4 14. Bd2 a3 15. b3 Rc8 16. Rac1 Ndb8 $2 {(The plan ?b8-a6-c7-b5-c3/d4 is too slow. Better to remain on d7, eyeing f6 & e5)} 17. Bh3 Na6 18. Ng5 Nd4 $2 (18... h6) 19. Qh5 Bxg5 $4 (19... h6 $1 $11) 20. Bxg5 Qe8 (20... f6 {is hardly ideal for Black but at least it does not lose immediately}) 21. Bf6 $18 h6 (21... gxf6 22. Ng4 {wins either the ? or ?!}) (21... Kh8 $145 {is Fritz 4.01's suggestion; there is just one clear-cut winning line for White after it, which is absolutely crushing:} 22. Bxg7+ $1 Kxg7 23. Qg5+ Kh8 24. Qf6+ Kg8 25. Ng4 h6 (25... Nf5 26. Qg5+ Kh8 27. Nf6 $18) 26. Nxh6+ $1 (26. Qxh6 $2 f5 27. Nf6+ Rxf6 28. exf6 Qf7 {is not all over by any means}) 26... Kh7 27. Ng4 Nf5 $8 28. Qg5 f6 29. Nxf6+ Rxf6 30. exf6 {with a number of unstoppable threats - editor}) 22. Ng4 Nf5 (22... Nf3+ 23. Kh1 d4 24. Nxh6+ $1 gxh6 25. Qxh6 {mating in 3 despite the juicy-looking discovered check}) 23. Nxh6+ {Source: Tom Middleton} (23. Nxh6+ $1 Nxh6 (23... gxh6 24. Bxf5 exf5 25. Qxh6 $18) 24. Qg5 Nf5 25. Bxf5 g6 26. Qh6 $18) 1-0

